# Inventory

## Daily onhand append (Cursor)

Umair appends a **full POS onhand snapshot** through Cursor (not a same-day row merge like sales). Always replace live inventory:

```
npx tsx scripts/append-onhand.ts <onhand.csv>
```

| File | Lands in |
|---|---|
| Daily onhand CSV | `data/inventory/Inventory-Onhand.csv` + `.data/inventory/` (calculator + sales onhand stay in sync) |

Normalize empty spacer columns; fill **Whole Cost** from Tag × CP divisor rules (`normalizeAndFillOnhandCsv`). **Do not** use Whole Cost as Kash’s transfer/onhand cost.

After write, script fails if the snapshot looks empty. Inventory Transfers / All on-hand read this file — no extra rebuild.

## Who sees Inventory

Nav + `/inventory` + `/api/inventory-mgmt`: **Kash, admin, Ross, Marina** only (`canAccessInventoryMgmt`). AJ / Shaun / others do not.

## Cost column (Transfers + All on-hand)

| Login | Source column |
|---|---|
| Kash / admin / Ross / Marina | **Individual Cost Value** (`costPrice`) |
| Everyone else (if they ever see it) | **Whole Cost** |

Never use sales CSV Profit or another sheet for this column.

## Stores

- **AJ + Shaun** selling stores only for transfer From/To. Adeel, Rozina/VIS, CON, WEB excluded.
- **MAIN** = warehouse. Show onhand qty (dropdown **top**, All on-hand filter + list). **Never** a transfer donor/destination. No sold. No A/B/C label. Not in Transfers store filter.
- Store badges: **A** and **New** only. No B/C labels.

## Ignore departments (inventory + transfers)

`BATTERY`, `TRAY`, `GIFT BOX`, `BULOV GIFT` / `BULOVA GIFT`, `MISC`, `ROLEX BOX` (department match). Do **not** drop Gift Cards or Bulova watches whose subclass is Battery.

## Transfers

- Keep **at least 1** of each vendor model at every selling store.
- Donor only if **onhand ≥ 2** and selling is **slow** (`sold * 2 < onhand`, e.g. 5/1–2 yes, 5/3 no). Never fall back to a healthy store. A stores never donate. MAIN never donates.
- Click a line → all stores’ onhand/sold for that vendor model; MAIN first, onhand only (sold = —).
- Columns: vendor model, description/department, To onhand/sold/store, From onhand/sold/store, tag, cost, sold revenue. No move-qty column.

## Implementation

- Engine: `src/lib/inventory/mgmt-engine.ts` + `mgmt-stores.ts`
- API: `GET /api/inventory-mgmt`
- Append: `scripts/append-onhand.ts` (alias `scripts/import-onhand.ts`)
- Parse: `Individual Cost Value` → `costPrice`, `Whole Cost` → `wholesaleCost` (`parse-csv.ts`)
